From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Nicolas Villar <15879262+nvillar@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 4 Nov 2026 02:18:41 -0800
Subject: [PATCH 1/3] Duo: restore a task minimized by Home when it is moved to
 front again

Home on a panel hid the panel's tasks with the task organizer's hidden reason, and only two places showed them again:
the end of panelForLaunch (after every early return, so not in a single panel posture, for a launch without source
bounds or from a non home caller) and moving a task to front inside a panel area. After a fold to a single panel a
relaunched app was reparented to the default task area, still hidden, and nothing was shown. Both places also cleared
FLAG_FORCE_HIDDEN_FOR_TASK_ORG, which belongs to Shell's task organizer.

- The policy hides with its own reason, FLAG_FORCE_HIDDEN_FOR_DUO_PANEL, and only ever clears that reason.
- A task is restored only when it is committed to the front of a task display area (positionChildTaskAt with
  moveToTop), in any task display area, not only in a panel. That is after ActivityStarter.isAllowedToStart() and
  only for launches that may move to front (background and avoidMoveToFront launches do not), and also covers
  recents and the reparent-to-default-area path after a fold (getOrCreateRootTask reparents, moveTaskToFront follows).
- A restore clears the flag on the positioned root and every task below it, and Task.onParentChanged drops the flag
  when a task is nested under another task (an organizer's launch root: Recents to split screen reparents through
  RootWindowContainer.anyTaskForId before the root is moved to front). The flag is only meaningful on a panel root
  task; a root task moved to another task display area keeps it until it is moved to front, so a background
  reparent (avoidMoveToFront) does not show it.
- panelForLaunch, which runs while launch params are computed, before the launch is allowed, no longer changes any
  task state; it only decides a panel.
- panelForLaunch leaves launches from an activity on another display alone (a home on an external display passes
  no display id), so explicit and external display launches keep the platform choice.

Not built or run on a device yet; part of the M1 gate prototype.

Co-authored-by: Copilot App <223556219+Copilot@users.noreply.github.com>
